review.summary:
The fix solves T-83. `_area_objects` now drops an object that lies inside the area's geometry when it has Total Cover from the point of origin. It finds the origin the same way `_area_targets` does for creatures: the caster for a Self-range spell, otherwise the point. It logs the exclusion with page=177 and rule="GLOSS.area-of-effect#3", matching the creature path.

The scene-label lookup is now its own method, `Game.labelled_cover`, and `cover_between` uses it too. The 'most protective degree applies' rule (PLAY.combat.cover#4) has moved into `_most_cover`, so it is still decided in one place and there is no second cover mechanism. Objects get only the label-based cover, which is right: a creature in the way gives at most Half Cover, so it can never block an area.

The xfail is removed only from the T-83 acceptance test, which now passes. The new unit tests check real behaviour:
- an object behind Total Cover is left out of the area;
- an object with only Three-Quarters Cover stays in;
- the exclusion event is logged;
- per-origin and blanket labels combine by the most protective degree.

Nothing in the diff is hard-coded or outside the ticket's scope.
